WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.107
ICU message format is a syntax
for one translatable string

2
00:00:05.107 --> 00:00:07.174
with variables, plurals,

3
00:00:07.174 --> 00:00:09.402
select choices, and ordinals.

4
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.099
English uses the plural
categories one and other,

5
00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:15.385
while Polish adds few and many.

6
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:20.237
General Translation's useGT
accepts an ICU message and its

7
00:00:20.237 --> 00:00:20.874
values.

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:26.005
Pass the count, and a $context
note that says where the message

9
00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:26.654
appears.

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.817
Then npx gt translate generates
a translation for each target

11
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:32.466
locale.

12
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.785
It uses $context, your Glossary,

13
00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:37.874
and Custom Prompts as context.

14
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.736
Your team now ships every plural
form in Polish with each release.
